1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,789
Same task, same repository.

2
00:00:01,789 --> 00:00:06,427
One run read one hundred seven thousand tokens and locked the session.

3
00:00:06,427 --> 00:00:08,613
The other read four hundred four.

4
00:00:08,613 --> 00:00:11,595
This was measured live in Google Antigravity.

5
00:00:11,595 --> 00:00:15,637
Here is what changed, how each run spent its tokens, and why.

6
00:00:16,437 --> 00:00:17,585
The result first.

7
00:00:17,585 --> 00:00:18,329
Bytes read:

8
00:00:18,329 --> 00:00:22,383
from four hundred seven thousand down to about one thousand.

9
00:00:22,383 --> 00:00:22,788
Lines:

10
00:00:22,788 --> 00:00:24,748
ten thousand down to sixteen.

11
00:00:24,748 --> 00:00:28,126
Input tokens, minus ninety nine point six percent.

12
00:00:28,126 --> 00:00:30,964
Output tokens, minus eighty three percent.

13
00:00:30,964 --> 00:00:32,248
Seven times faster.

14
00:00:32,248 --> 00:00:34,747
And the optimised run ended verified.

15
00:00:34,747 --> 00:00:37,450
The baseline ended with nothing checked.

16
00:00:38,250 --> 00:00:40,766
The test was one real task, run twice.

17
00:00:40,766 --> 00:00:46,326
Check one progress sheet against the rules of its area, and validate
the repository.

18
00:00:46,326 --> 00:00:46,855
Run one:

19
00:00:46,855 --> 00:00:49,768
a single big model, no routing, whole files.

20
00:00:49,768 --> 00:00:50,297
Run two:

21
00:00:50,297 --> 00:00:52,415
the scaffolding from this guide.

22
00:00:53,216 --> 00:00:55,437
How the baseline spent its tokens.

23
00:00:55,437 --> 00:00:56,025
Step one:

24
00:00:56,025 --> 00:00:57,659
it loads whole documents.

25
00:00:57,659 --> 00:00:58,900
Ten thousand lines.

26
00:00:58,900 --> 00:00:59,488
Step two:

27
00:00:59,488 --> 00:01:04,324
all of it lands in a single turn, one hundred seven thousand input
tokens.

28
00:01:04,324 --> 00:01:05,042
Step three:

29
00:01:05,042 --> 00:01:10,597
that one turn already exceeds the free plan context limit, so the
session is blocked.

30
00:01:10,597 --> 00:01:12,949
And even then, nothing was verified.

31
00:01:13,749 --> 00:01:16,192
How the optimised run spent its tokens.

32
00:01:16,192 --> 00:01:16,755
Step one:

33
00:01:16,755 --> 00:01:17,319
the gate.

34
00:01:17,319 --> 00:01:21,014
The task is not fully specified, so it goes to the planner.

35
00:01:21,014 --> 00:01:21,578
Step two:

36
00:01:21,578 --> 00:01:22,706
a surgical lookup.

37
00:01:22,706 --> 00:01:26,213
One grep, sixteen lines, four hundred four input tokens.

38
00:01:26,213 --> 00:01:26,902
Step three:

39
00:01:26,902 --> 00:01:30,159
the planner writes a Work Order, seventy six tokens.

40
00:01:30,159 --> 00:01:30,785
Step four:

41
00:01:30,785 --> 00:01:37,237
the low tier agent runs the audit script, finds no broken links, and
closes with DONE in twenty tokens.

42
00:01:38,037 --> 00:01:40,280
The whole ledger fits on one slide.

43
00:01:40,280 --> 00:01:42,075
Four hundred four tokens in.

44
00:01:42,075 --> 00:01:44,639
Seventy six tokens out from the planner.

45
00:01:44,639 --> 00:01:46,690
Twenty out from the cheap agent.

46
00:01:46,690 --> 00:01:52,202
Ninety six output tokens in total, and zero point four percent of the
free plan quota.

47
00:01:53,002 --> 00:01:54,310
Was the theory right?

48
00:01:54,310 --> 00:01:59,293
Before the live test, the estimate said about ninety to a hundred
output tokens.

49
00:01:59,293 --> 00:01:59,854
Measured:

50
00:01:59,854 --> 00:02:00,539
ninety six.

51
00:02:00,539 --> 00:02:05,460
Reads and input came in lower than predicted, so the estimate was
conservative.

52
00:02:05,460 --> 00:02:07,204
Time was the loosest number:

53
00:02:07,204 --> 00:02:10,069
the run was three times faster than predicted.

54
00:02:10,869 --> 00:02:11,986
Why it is cheaper.

55
00:02:11,986 --> 00:02:16,145
The saving comes from reading less, not from a cheaper model alone.

56
00:02:16,145 --> 00:02:21,793
Input fell about ninety nine point six percent because of the gate and
the surgical lookup.

57
00:02:21,793 --> 00:02:26,386
One big source file can cost about eighty eight thousand tokens by
itself.

58
00:02:26,386 --> 00:02:28,682
Read sixteen lines, not ten thousand.

59
00:02:29,482 --> 00:02:33,599
The output saving comes from separating planning from execution.

60
00:02:33,599 --> 00:02:36,686
The planner writes seventy six tokens and stops.

61
00:02:36,686 --> 00:02:39,966
The cheap agent does the mechanical part in twenty.

62
00:02:39,966 --> 00:02:46,720
And a deterministic command ends the task with an explicit status,
instead of long prose nobody verified.

63
00:02:47,520 --> 00:02:51,517
Over three task types, the analytical estimate says the same story.

64
00:02:51,517 --> 00:02:52,293
Input tokens:

65
00:02:52,293 --> 00:02:55,396
two hundred fifty two thousand down to two thousand.

66
00:02:55,396 --> 00:02:56,410
High tier output:

67
00:02:56,410 --> 00:02:59,214
eleven thousand down to two hundred forty five.

68
00:02:59,214 --> 00:03:00,408
Twelve times faster.

69
00:03:00,408 --> 00:03:04,525
Four errors down to zero, because the gate blocks the ambiguous task.

70
00:03:04,525 --> 00:03:08,284
In the baseline, the free plan quota was exhausted by turn two.

71
00:03:08,284 --> 00:03:08,880
Optimised:

72
00:03:08,880 --> 00:03:10,730
about three and a half percent.

73
00:03:11,530 --> 00:03:12,433
Honest limits.

74
00:03:12,433 --> 00:03:15,593
The live test covers a single documentation task.

75
00:03:15,593 --> 00:03:19,397
The refactor and the ambiguous debug results are estimates.

76
00:03:19,397 --> 00:03:21,138
Quota depends on your plan.

77
00:03:21,138 --> 00:03:25,781
Treat the shape of the result as reliable, and measure your own
numbers.

78
00:03:26,581 --> 00:03:27,331
So do this.

79
00:03:27,331 --> 00:03:28,286
Gate the task.

80
00:03:28,286 --> 00:03:30,740
Grep one section, never whole files.

81
00:03:30,740 --> 00:03:33,263
Let the planner write the Work Order.

82
00:03:33,263 --> 00:03:36,673
Let a cheap agent run the check and end with DONE.

83
00:03:36,673 --> 00:03:40,355
The full tables are in scaffold E N dot p d f, part E.

84
00:03:40,355 --> 00:03:41,514
Go measure yours.

